Marvel might rule the cinema today but  before the MCU is king they release some  real stinkers animatronic ducks multiple  attempts at a Fantastic Four franchise  and Nicolas Cage and leather Marvel's  failures are legion these are the Marvel  movies that flopped at the box office  unlike most of the films on this list  blade Trinity actually did fairly well  at the box office  unfortunately the key word there is  fairly after the success of the first  two films in the saga Marvel's vampire  slaying daywalker blade Trinity's budget  was bumped up far beyond its  predecessors despite the extra cash in a  plot involving vampire dogs played  Trinity made almost exactly the same  amount as the first blade film did about  a hundred and thirty 1 million dollars  that was a huge profit for a surprise  hit made on a budget of seventeen  million but a little less than they  hoped for with Trinity's 65 million  dollar budget blade 2 also had a smaller  budget than blade Trinity but it made  about twenty million dollars more making  it clear that blade was daywalking  himself writing to some diminishing  returns  because the world is nice the  behind-the-scenes drama was ramping up  as well one particularly infamous story  involves star Wesley Snipes strangling  the film's director David s Goyer in  front of the crew and that's what's  going on behind the scenes it's no  wonder the producers started to think  that the Prophet Trinity brought in just  wasn't enough for the producers to deal  with the headache of making more blade  films blade is reportedly getting a  reboot into the MCU with more ursula  elise at the start let's hope he keeps  to the scripted violence and skips the  director strangling it's hard to imagine  what Marvel was thinking when they  decided that the first feature-length  film based on one of their comics should  be Howard the Duck to be fair Howard was  sort of the Deadpool of his day a comedy  oddball in the superhero universe that  frequently broke the fourth wall the  film which was jointly produced by  Lucasfilm and Marvel is generally  regarded as being a hot mess there's an  odd ickiness to the whole affair  starting with Howard's romance with  Beverly which asked audiences to be  totally cool with watching a duck hook  up with a very human lady  maybe Lea Thompson was trying to find  the one love scene that would be even  ski beour than the one she got when she  kissed Marty and back to the future  the plot is meandering the jokes never  quite land there's really no shortage of  reasons the film barely made back its  budget of 37 million dollars  interestingly Howard the Duck is  actually part of the Marvel Cinematic  Universe already thanks to a couple of  cameos we wouldn't bet on another  starring role anytime soon though this  is another bomb that comes with an  asterisk  Ghost Rider spirit of vengeance the  second film starring what is arguably  the world's most famous on fire skeleton  that rides a motorcycle and punishes  sinners ultimately didn't do terribly at  the box office it wound up bringing in  132 million dollars against the 57  million dollar budget however a few red  flags went up with this one that landed  solidly in the flop category for one  thing spirit of vengeance made nearly a  hundred million dollars less than the  first Ghost Rider film that's a huge  drop-off especially considering the  films were released only a few years  apart secondly the domestic take in  particular went down significantly which  mattered a lot more in 2011 than it  might today one other factor is an  extremely technical element known to  filmmakers as Nicolas Cage  cage was one of the most marketable  movie stars around the late 1990s and  early 2000s but somewhere near 2010 the  backlash began as cage started taking  more questionable roles admittedly  starring in a supernatural superhero  movie directed by the two guys who made  the wildly fun over-the-top  prank films probably seemed like a safer  bet who knew the audiences would be the  ones wanting vengeance when this one  turned out to be so bad  The Incredible Hulk is considered one of  the few missteps Marvel made with their  phase 1 films Edward Norton seemed like  a slam-dunk pick as Bruce Banner and  you'll certainly find his vocal backers  around the internet especially in video  comment sections but Mark Ruffalo has  really taken the role of Hulk / banner  and made its own on paper The Incredible  Hulk is hardly a bomb and almost made  back its 150 million dollar budget and  ultimately brought in another 129  million dollars for a worldwide gross of  264 million dollars it does not however  come close to replicating the success of  Iron Man Robert Downey jr. first MCU  film blew audiences away and raked in  nearly six hundred million dollars and  that was with a smaller budget than the  Incredible Hulk it's not hard to see why  this one was a bit of a disappointment  for the brass in 2007 the trend of  big-budget superhero movies was just  starting to ramp up the x-men and  spider-man franchises had brought in  hundreds of millions of dollars and  Batman Begins proved that DC could  revive their biggest characters with a  popular critical hit - fans were also  gearing up for the following year which  would see the Dark Knight and a movie  star in one of Marvel's most enduring  fiy Lister's Iron Man that looked like  it might be fun Fantastic Four rise of  the Silver Surfer a sequel to the first  FF movie in 2005 that was adapting one  of the most groundbreaking and beloved  stories in comics history was in the  perfect spot to be a smash hit for  Marvel's first family all things  considered rise of the Silver Surfer  wasn't that bad when it came to  profitability the film at a massive 130  million dollar budget but ultimately  landed at a worldwide gross of 301  million dollars not bad until you see it  stacked up against other superhero  franchises like the spider-man films  which brought in over twice as much rise  of the Silver Surfer was definitely a  financial disappointment it didn't fare  better with fans either confronted with  the challenge of creating a big screen  tation of Galactus the planet jumping  devourer of worlds the filmmakers  decided to ditch the classic comic book  look and make him something much less  silly a cloud a really mean cloud after  this release it's no surprise that  Hollywood bigwigs decided that ffs just  couldn't hack it with the big voice and  put them back on the Shelf it would be  years before they would return for  another shot leading to the equally  disastrous 2015 Fantastic Four movie we  probably should have seen this one  coming though come on Chris Evans who  whatever buy that guy is a superhero  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff or coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

